# Write documentation components

Use `:name[params]` for bounded documentation components. The parser stores the
kind, optional params, and body; Rocdown validates the content model; the theme
paints the HTML. Fenced code stays display-only.

:note[title: "Static pages"] {{
    Rocdown accepts `:note` next to Markdown and `@page` on `static` site pages.
    `@render`, `@component`, and other islands belong on `hydrate` or `live`
    pages, not inside a `:note` body.
}}

## Call out a risk

:caution {{
    Do not paste raw HTML into Markdown. Use a component when the page needs
    structure beyond CommonMark.
}}

## Walk through a procedure

:steps.begin
    :step[title: "Author the block"] {{
        Start a document-root line with `:`, then the kind. Params go in `[]`.
        Content is the rest of the line, `{{ }}`, or `:kind.begin` ...
        `:kind.end`. Nested blocks are allowed. Do not mix `.begin` with
        double braces on the same call.
    }}

    :step[title: "Include source from disk", verify: Bool.true] {{
        Point `:include` at a file under the content root. Prefer a named
        region over line numbers.
    }}
:steps.end

:include[path: "snippets/hello.rs", region: "hello", language: "rust"]

## Show alternatives without JavaScript

Every tab panel is in the document. Print, forced-colors, and browsers with
scripts disabled show all panels. There is no `tablist` role until a hashed
script exists. `:tabs` bodies may contain only `:tab` children; stray
Markdown or other blocks are errors.

:tabs.begin[group: "install", kind: "tool"]
    :tab[id: "cli", label: "CLI"] {{
        Check the catalog without compiling Roc:

        ```sh
        cargo run -p rocci-rocdown-cli -- check site
        ```
    }}

    :tab[id: "test", label: "Examples"] {{
        Run declared example commands. This is not part of `rocdown build`.

        ```sh
        cargo run -p rocci-rocdown-cli -- test site
        ```
    }}
:tabs.end

