}}

:example[id: "echo-hello", language: "sh", test: ["/bin/echo", "hello"], expect: "hello"] {{
    ```sh
    echo hello
    ```
}}

## Replace painters or add a site kind

A site `theme/Blocks.rocci` (or `theme/blocks/*.rocci`) overlays builtin painters
by exporting the same `@component` names. A new PascalCase export becomes a
custom static kind (`Callout` → `:callout`). Helpers must not live in that pack.
`@use` stays interactive-only; static `rocdown build` does not honor it. See
[Rocdown site configuration](/docs/reference/rocdown-site/).

```rocci
import Html

@component Note = |{ title }, content|
    <section data-callout data-title={title}>{content}</section>

@component Callout = |{ tone ?? "note" }, content|
    <aside data-tone={tone}>{content}</aside>
```

```rocdown
:note[title: "Watch"] Body still uses `:note`.

:callout[tone: "warn"] {{
    Custom kinds work only on sites that compile that pack.
}}
```

`api-operation` is reserved for generated API reference and is rejected until
that work ships.
